## 6. Editor ↔ server protocol

```
client → server  { type: "create_project", name, description?, sceneName? }   // also creates and opens the first scene
client → server  { type: "update_project", project, name?, description? }
client → server  { type: "create_scene", project, name }                     // opens it
client → server  { type: "rename_scene", project, scene, name }
client → server  { type: "duplicate_scene", project, scene, name? }          // opens the copy
client → server  { type: "open_scene", project, scene }
client → server  { type: "set_view", view, camera }                          // camera = { focus, yaw, distance } (new)
                 (every scene edit, set_selection, undo / redo / clear unchanged; they fail with an error while nothing is open)

server → client  { type: "projects", projects: [{ id, name, description, scenes: [{ id, name, error? }] }] }
                   // on connect, and broadcast whenever the list changes
server → client  { type: "opened", project: { id, name, description } | null, scene: { id, name } | null, camera?, selection? }
                   // on connect, and broadcast when the open scene changes; the editor restores camera and selection only here
server → client  scene (+ history), error                                    // unchanged
```

