## 10. Acceptance test (end of phase)

1. Stop the server, move `./data` aside, start it. The editor shows the create project form and can't be dismissed. `get_scene` from the agent returns the "no scene open" error.
2. Create "Castle" with a description and a first scene "Entrance". The bar shows **Castle ▸ Entrance**, and `data/projects/castle/scenes/entrance/` exists, along with `abilities/`, `entities/` and `rules/`.
3. Draw three rooms. Ask the agent to add a pillar in the middle one. `get_scene` shows the project, its description and the scene.
4. Pan, rotate, zoom, and select a room. Restart the server and reload the page. The same scene, boxes, camera and selection come back.
5. `⌘Z` removes the pillar, and `⌘Z` again removes the last room. `⌘⇧Z` twice brings both back. The labels match the steps (`Agent: draw box_4`).
6. Draw one more box. It gets the next ID, never a reused one.
7. Picker: create scene "Crypt" and draw in it. The agent sees the crypt only. Go back to "Entrance": its boxes, camera and undo history are its own.
8. Duplicate "Entrance" as "Entrance B" and move a room in the copy. "Entrance" is unchanged. `⌘Z` in the copy works back through the history it inherited.
9. Rename "Crypt" to "Catacombs". The folder stays `crypt/`, and the new name survives a restart.
10. Two tabs: opening a scene in one switches the other.
11. Start a second server on `:5171` with no `DATA_DIR`. It refuses to start because `./data` is locked.

